er/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-82952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{56.22}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/state.json" "file_sha256" "84fde27b1a00a1294e05039b91d97dabd7d2c4c9c595263f4404be9a9a9ee789" "basis" 1915 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-82952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{49.11}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/state.json" "file_sha256" "84fde27b1a00a1294e05039b91d97dabd7d2c4c9c595263f4404be9a9a9ee789" "basis" 1915 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/state.json" "file_sha256" "84fde27b1a00a1294e05039b91d97dabd7d2c4c9c595263f4404be9a9a9ee789" "basis" 1915 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/state.json" "file_sha256" "84fde27b1a00a1294e05039b91d97dabd7d2c4c9c595263f4404be9a9a9ee789" "basis" 1915 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b5954bff8b5541ae3978022ac0c3d32b2